{
  "_comment": "Adventurers (adventurers/Adventurers.PlayerBots.js): a few named bots that start as new accounts and play on their own, training toward the quests below and completing them. Their progress is saved. quests: the order they take quests in, by the quest's name as registered on this server; skills and quests are extra requirements on top of the cache's quest table (Quests.PlayerBots.js), combat a recommended combat level. Every other quest on the server follows, easiest first. A quest is done only where a bot playthrough is built (playthrough: true); nothing is simulated, so without one they skip it. trainMinutes / questMinutes: how long one stretch lasts. questChance: the chance to pick a quest when one is ready. groupChance: the chance an adventurer takes the others along (Wintertodt together, or the same training spot). dropValue: the lowest value (coins) of a drop that goes in the drop log. bossLevel: the lowest combat level of a kill that goes in the boss log. bosses: the bosses adventurers fight from their combat level, in the boss's shared lair (x, y: where they arrive); bossChance: the chance to go bossing when one is open to them, alone or with the others. generation: raise it to start every adventurer over (levels, items, quests and journal reset, with the Tutorial Island starter kit). grandExchange: where they sell (the Grand Exchange's centre). focus: per adventurer, how much more it likes a mode (2 = twice as often) when nothing else decides. shopRadius: they walk to a shop only within this many tiles (a longer walk is not worth one item). Everything is on foot (brain/Errands.PlayerBots.js). bankCap, bankKeep, junkValue: what they keep in the bank for later (their training materials and these), up to bankCap each (the surplus is sold); unwearable things worth under junkValue each they drop. buyToTrain: skills they may train on bought materials when they can pay (the best tier their level allows, `amount` of it at the Grand Exchange; the product is sold again, often at a loss, as players do to train). banks: where they bank the last job's things; sellValue: from this much, or when the Grand Exchange is about as near, they sell instead (and take banked goods along as notes). keepValue: goods worth less than this stay in its bag between stretches (otherwise it sells them first); fullSlots: or when this few slots are free. Coins only come from sales and finds (adventurers/Trade.PlayerBots.js).",
